<section class="section__wrapper">
  <section id="faq" class="section__content">
    <!-- <div class="headline-wrapper"> -->
    <h1 class="faq__title">
      <span class="section__content--dark-text">Find the answers<br /></span>
      <span class="section__content--white-text">to your questions</span>
    </h1>
    <!-- </div> -->
    <!-- <div class="faq-wrapper"> -->
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">
          We have a Facebook page. Why do we need a professional website?
        </h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          Relying solely on a social media platform is a bit like building a
          house on rented land - you don’t actually own the property, and the
          landlord can change the rules at any time. Having a professional
          website shows your organisation is established and professional.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">
          Why can’t I just do it myself using a website builder?
        </h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          You absolutely can build your own website using tools like
          Squarespace, Wix, or Shopify.<br />However, the "DIY vs. Professional"
          debate isn't just about whether you can do it - it’s about the
          opportunity cost and the invisible technical gaps. Building a decent
          website yourself typically takes 40 to 100 hours of learning,
          troubleshooting, and design.<br />Also, many website builders are
          "closed systems. If you want to retrieve your information and move
          elsewhere, you often can't just export your site.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">
          I have seen a website design I like. Can you build something similar
          for me?
        </h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          Absolutely! If you describe the website or share specific details
          about it, I can identify and replicate the layout, reverse-engineer
          its features and match its fonts and colours.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">
          What is the cost of designing and building a modern website?
        </h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          When hiring a professional to build a modern, bespoke website for you,
          you are paying for expertise and time.<br />The cost will depend
          entirely on whether you are building a simple digital business card or
          a high-performance piece of online real estate.<br /> A small club website
          might cost around $1000, whereas one with added functionality, like a membership
          signup system, might cost proportionately more.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">
          How long does it take to complete a typical project?
        </h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          Typically, a one-page website takes 1 to 2 weeks to complete, although
          I have built some faster than that.
          <br />A website with 6 to 8 pages normally takes 4 to 6 weeks to go
          live. However, in practice, factors like the content bottleneck (text
          and photos not yet available) or custom features may extend the
          timeline.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">What content do I need to provide?</h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          Essentially two things – the words and the assets.<br />The words
          include both text for the pages and things like captions for photos.<br
          />The assets include good quality photos and documents such as
          membership application forms or policies.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">
          Do you offer support and maintenance after launch?
        </h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          All projects include free support and maintenance for a short period
          to fix any bugs or issues that may arise immediately after launch.<br
          />
          Following this, a support and maintenance package will be quoted for separately.
          This includes content updates, plugin updates, site backups, feature enhancements
          and performance tuning.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="question__header">
        <svg
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="question__icon"
          ><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19" class=""></line>
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" class=""></line></svg
        >
        <h5 class="question__text">Will my information be safe?</h5>
      </div>
      <div class="question-content">
        <h5 class="answer">
          Website security is no longer a "luxury" feature—it is a standard
          requirement.<br />While no system on the internet is 100% unhackable,
          a modern professional website is significantly more secure than a
          Facebook page.<br />All Mart.I.N’s websites include an SSL Certificate
          (HTTPS). This creates an encrypted "tunnel" between your visitor's
          browser and your server to ensure privacy.
        </h5>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- </div> -->
  </section>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  .section__wrapper {
    background: var(--pure-accent-teal);
    padding-bottom: 4em;
  }
  .faq__title {
    margin-bottom: 1em;
    padding-top: 1em;
    transition: all 0.5s;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 4em;
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.4em;
  }
  .question {
    &__header {
      font-size: 1.2em;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      cursor: pointer;
      outline: none;
      text-align: left;
      width: 100%;
    }
    &__icon {
      align-self: center;
    }
    &__text {
      margin-left: 0.5em;
      font-family: "Montserrat", sans-serif;
    }
  }
  .faq .question-content {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease;
  }
  .faq.active .question-content {
    max-height: 500px;
  }
  .faq.active .question__header > svg {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }
  h5.answer {
    font-family: "Montserrat", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1em;
    font-weight: normal;
    margin-top: 0.5em;
    color: var(--pure-neutral-light);
    line-height: 1.5em;
  }
</style>
<script>
  import { onScroll, animate, stagger } from "animejs";
  function animateFAQ() {
    animate(".faq", {
      y: [50, 0],
      opacity: [0, 1],
      // scale: [0, 1],
      // ease: "InOutExpo",
      delay: stagger(400, {
        start: 100,
      }),
      autoplay: onScroll({
        sync: "play play play reset",
        enter: "max bottom",
        leave: "min top",
      }),
    });
  }
  animateFAQ();

  // // FAQ Accordion
  document.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    const button = (e.target as Element).closest(".question__header");
    if (button) {
      const accordionItem = button.closest(".faq");
      const allItems = document.querySelectorAll(".faq");

      allItems.forEach((item) => {
        if (item !== accordionItem) {
          item.classList.remove("active");
        }
      });

      accordionItem.classList.toggle("active");
      console.log(accordionItem.classList);
    }
  });
</script>
